# SIM Inventory Import — build spec

Action-by-action. Build top to bottom; every action's name matters because later
expressions reference it.

**Naming rule:** Power Automate turns spaces into underscores in expressions. Name an action
`Get inventory` and you reference it as `body('Get_inventory')`. Use the exact names below.

---

## 0. Before you start

Three things that aren't actions but will cost you a day if missed.

**Index the SharePoint columns you filter on.** List settings → Indexed columns → add
`SIM_Country`. Without it, `Get items` with a filter fails past 5,000 items with the list view
threshold error. Also index `ICC_ID` if you ever filter on it.

**Set trigger concurrency to 1.** Settings on the trigger → Concurrency Control → On → Degree
of parallelism `1`. Two people importing the same country simultaneously will both read the
inventory *before* either writes, so both decide "create" for the same row and you get
duplicates. This is the single most likely way to corrupt the list.

**Create two libraries:** `SIM Imports/Staging` for uploaded workbooks and `SIM Imports/Reports`
for the HTML. Keep them out of the library holding the master template.

