## 2. Initialize variables

These must sit at the **root of the flow**. Power Automate refuses `Initialize variable`
inside a Scope, Condition or loop, which is why they can't be bundled with anything else.

| Name | Type | Value |
|---|---|---|
| `varRunId` | String | `guid()` |
| `varFileName` | String | `concat(formatDateTime(utcNow(),'yyyy-MM-dd_HH-mm-ss'),'_',triggerBody()?['text'],'_SIM_Import_',substring(variables('varRunId'),0,8),'.xlsx')` |
| `varPage` | Integer | `0` |
| `varHasMore` | Boolean | `true` |
| `varReportRows` | Array | `[]` |
| `varCreated` / `varUpdated` / `varWarning` / `varSkipped` / `varFailed` | Integer | `0` |
| `varBatchFailures` | Array | `[]` |
| `varStatus` | String | `Running` |

Separate integer counters rather than one object variable — Power Automate can't increment a
property inside an object, so a single `varCounts` object means rebuilding the whole thing on
every page.

