## 7. Build the report

- **`Compose report meta`**

```json
{
  "fileName": "@{variables('varFileName')}",
  "country": "@{triggerBody()?['text']}",
  "runId": "@{variables('varRunId')}",
  "startedUtc": "@{triggerBody()?['headers']?['x-ms-workflow-run-start-time']}",
  "finishedUtc": "@{utcNow()}",
  "operator": "@{triggerBody()?['text_2']}",
  "listName": "SIM Inventory",
  "gate": "@{if(equals(variables('varFailed'),0),'OK','BLOCKED')}"
}
```

- **`Compose report json`** — `{ "meta": @{outputs('Compose_report_meta')}, "rows": @{union(variables('varReportRows'), variables('varBatchFailures'))} }`
- **`Get report template`** — SharePoint → Get file content, `Import_Report_Template.html`
- **`Compose report html`**

```
replace(base64ToString(body('Get_report_template')?['$content']), '__REPORT_JSON__', string(outputs('Compose_report_json')))
```

- **`Save report`** — Create file in `/SIM Imports/Reports`, name `replace(variables('varFileName'),'.xlsx','.html')`

Saving as well as emailing gives you a permanent link, and a fallback when the attachment is
stripped by a mail gateway.

